# interplay_limits_displays_reset: All eight display ports (RVG_MAX_DISPLAY_PORTS) busy at once, each display offering 130 modes (the page lists 128), each connected and acked, given the largest cursor glyph (256 x 256; a 256 KiB glyph written with mem_seq) and shown, and presented with the largest gamma table (1024 entries), while tasks 1-8 run execs on children 1-8. Then tasks 1-8 queue execs on their children gated on a root stamp that never comes, and the host resets: the teardown disconnects all eight guest displays (eight interrupts; ports 0 and 7 read mode count 0) and drops the children and tasks with their waits, but leaves the task words in the root page as they were (the display words are cleared). Brought up again on the same pages, port 7 reconnects and presents, and child 1 with task 1 runs again. The children's block calls (blocks setup) interleave with the root's by timing, and are locked sorted.
